-- s 68. The insurer's s 64(2) notice was given on Monday 1 March 2027; the 21st day after is Monday 22 March 2027.
#ASSERT `By when can I object to their hearsay notice question` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 22 3 2027) (`the calendar date` 30 3 2027) EQUALS `in time: I took the step within 21 days after the notice or service`
#ASSERT `By when can I object to their hearsay notice question` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 23 3 2027) (`the calendar date` 30 3 2027) EQUALS `too late: the 21 days have passed`
#ASSERT `By when can I object to their hearsay notice question` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `in time: I took the step within 21 days after the notice or service`
#ASSERT `By when can I object to their hearsay notice question` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2027) (`the calendar date` 10 3 2027) EQUALS `still open` (`the calendar date` 22 3 2027)
#ASSERT `By when can I object to their hearsay notice question` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2027) (`the calendar date` 22 3 2027) EQUALS `still open` (`the calendar date` 22 3 2027)
#ASSERT `By when can I object to their hearsay notice question` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2027) (`the calendar date` 23 3 2027) EQUALS `too late: the 21 days have passed`
-- A notice that does not rely on undue expense, delay or impracticability gives no s 68 objection.
#ASSERT `By when can I object to their hearsay notice question` FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2027) (`the calendar date` 10 3 2027) EQUALS `s 68 gives no objection: the other side's notice does not say they will not call the person because of undue expense or delay or impracticability`

-- s 168. The employer served a copy of a timesheet on Tuesday 5 January 2027; the 21st day after is Tuesday 26 January 2027.
#ASSERT `By when can I make my request question` `a served copy of a document they will tender` (`the calendar date` 5 1 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 26 1 2027) (`the calendar date` 1 2 2027) FALSE EQUALS `in time: I took the step within 21 days after the notice or service`
#ASSERT `By when can I make my request question` `a served copy of a document they will tender` (`the calendar date` 5 1 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 27 1 2027) (`the calendar date` 1 2 2027) FALSE EQUALS `too late: the 21 days have passed`
#ASSERT `By when can I make my request question` `a served copy of a document they will tender` (`the calendar date` 5 1 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 27 1 2027) (`the calendar date` 1 2 2027) TRUE EQUALS `too late, but the court has given me leave for good reason (s 168(2), (4), (7))`
-- Leave does not change an answer that was in time.
#ASSERT `By when can I make my request question` `a served copy of a document they will tender` (`the calendar date` 5 1 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 20 1 2027) (`the calendar date` 1 2 2027) TRUE EQUALS `in time: I took the step within 21 days after the notice or service`
-- Notice of the driver's conviction given 1 March 2027; no request yet on 15 March: open until 22 March.
#ASSERT `By when can I make my request question` `notice that they will use a person's conviction to prove a fact in issue` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2027) (`the calendar date` 15 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `still open` (`the calendar date` 22 3 2027)
-- Hearsay notice given 10 February 2027 (21st day after: 3 March 2027); request on 3 March: in time; nothing by 4 March: too late.
#ASSERT `By when can I make my request question` `notice that they will use a previous representation (hearsay)` (`the calendar date` 10 2 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2027) (`the calendar date` 5 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `in time: I took the step within 21 days after the notice or service`
#ASSERT `By when can I make my request question` `notice that they will use a previous representation (hearsay)` (`the calendar date` 10 2 2027) FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2027) (`the calendar date` 4 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `too late: the 21 days have passed`

-- s 169.
#ASSERT `What can the court do about my request question` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the court may, on my application, order them to comply, to produce the document or thing or call the person, that their evidence not be admitted, or as to adjournment or costs (s 169(1)); if they ignore an order to comply or produce, it may exclude their evidence (s 169(3))`
#ASSERT `What can the court do about my request question` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the court may, on my application, order them to comply, to produce the document or thing or call the person, that their evidence not be admitted, or as to adjournment or costs (s 169(1)); if they ignore an order to comply or produce, it may exclude their evidence (s 169(3))`
#ASSERT `What can the court do about my request question` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no order: they told me within a reasonable time that they refuse, and my application was not made within a reasonable time after that (s 169(2))`
#ASSERT `What can the court do about my request question` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no order under s 169(1): the court finds they had reasonable cause (for example the document is not available, its existence and contents are not in issue, or the person is not available, s 169(4))`
#ASSERT `What can the court do about my request question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing yet: they have not failed or refused to comply with my request`

